<section class="section" aria-labelledby="stages-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 id="stages-title">Who holds what, at each stage</h2>
      <p>Most sites describe a process. The questions that matter are who has your details, who is responsible for the work, and who you pay.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="data-table-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="Enquiry stages table, scrolls sideways on small screens">
      <table class="data-table stage-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">What happens</th><th scope="col">Who has your details</th><th scope="col">Who is responsible for the work</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">1. Enquiry</th><td>You describe the work, by phone or, once it opens, by {% routeLink "/request-an-accountant/", "the enquiry form" %}.</td><td>AccountOrbit</td><td>No one yet. Nothing has been agreed.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">2. Review</th><td>We look at what kind of professional the work calls for, including whether it is reserved for a particular qualification.</td><td>AccountOrbit</td><td>No one yet.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">3. Introduction</th><td>If someone suitable is available and you have agreed, we introduce you.</td><td>AccountOrbit, and the professional being considered</td><td>No one yet. An introduction is not an engagement.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">4. Your checks</th><td>You check their credentials and ask for the scope and fee in writing.</td><td>As above</td><td>No one yet. You can stop here.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">5. Engagement</th><td>If you choose to go ahead, you and the professional agree terms directly.</td><td>You and the professional decide what is shared next</td><td>The professional, for the work they accept. You remain responsible for your own filings and records.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="not-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="not-title">What AccountOrbit does not do</h2>
      <ul class="tick-list tick-list--no plain-list">
        <li>Prepare or file your accounts or returns</li>
        <li>Give personal tax or legal advice</li>
        <li>Conduct or sign audits</li>
        <li>Represent you before a tax authority</li>
        <li>Set a professional's fee</li>
        <li>Ask for passwords or OTPs</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>What is not yet settled</h2>
      <p>This platform is at an early stage, and these parts must be decided before it opens. We would rather show them to you than paper over them.</p>
      <dl class="open-points">
        <div><dt>Who pays AccountOrbit</dt><dd>{% pending "whether enquiries are free, and whether professionals pay AccountOrbit." %}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>How quickly you hear back</dt><dd>{% pending "who reviews enquiries and how soon." %}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>If no one suitable is available</dt><dd>No introduction is made. {% pending "how and when you are told." %}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>How professionals are checked</dt><dd>No checking procedure has been set, so we do not describe anyone as verified or screened. Please check credentials yourself.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

