      <p>A referral platform is one route, and it will not suit everyone. Typical differences are below; individual businesses vary, so check the one you are considering.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="data-table-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="Comparison of options, scrolls sideways on small screens">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Option</th><th scope="col">Who does the work</th><th scope="col">You would choose it when</th><th scope="col">Worth checking</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Referral platform</th><td>A separate professional</td><td>You are not sure what kind of help you need</td><td>Who receives your details, and who pays the platform</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Accounting or CA firm directly</th><td>That firm</td><td>You already know who you want</td><td>Credentials, who actually handles your file, and scope</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Directory</th><td>Whoever you contact</td><td>You want to compare many names yourself</td><td>Whether listings are paid, and whether reviews can be checked</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Online filing service</th><td>That company or its network</td><td>The task is standard and one-off</td><td>What is included, and who is accountable if it goes wrong</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Hiring an accountant</th><td>Your employee</td><td>You have enough regular work for a salaried role</td><td>Reserved work may still need an outside professional</td></tr>
